%% DM26-0670

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant B as Broker
    participant T as Transport
    participant F as Facade + Outbox
    participant R as Router
    participant D as Domain actor

    B->>T: PublishResponse(topic, payload, published_by, origin epoch and seq, delivery id)
    T->>F: Delivered(...)
    F->>F: origin (publisher, epoch, seq) already seen? yes: skip delivery and acknowledge again
    F->>R: Route(topic, payload)
    R->>D: deliver to the topic's registered handler
    F->>T: PublishResponseAck(delivery id)
    T->>B: PublishResponseAck(delivery id)
    B->>B: remove the delivery from this subscriber's outbox
    Note over B,F: If the connection fails before the acknowledgement, the broker keeps the delivery<br/>and sends it again after the reconnect. The facade drops the duplicate by its origin<br/>and acknowledges it again.
